# Build outputs must never enter the image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` and then runs `./gradlew :app:bootJar`. Without
# this file the build context carries ~250 MB of previous output — including
# app/build/libs/app.jar — and Gradle's up-to-date checks can conclude the jar
# is current and skip the build. The image then ships whatever was compiled on
# someone's machine last week, with no error anywhere.
#
# The Gradle wrapper JAR is the one build artifact that MUST be copied: without
# it there is no ./gradlew to run. It is explicitly re-included below.

.git
.gradle/
.kotlin/
build/
*/build/

# Editor / OS noise
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Local state and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
db/
docs/

# Not needed to build the jar
README.md
AGENTS.md
Caddyfile
check.sh
justfile
.just/

# Re-include what the build genuinely needs.
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties